The file "ablation_results_formatted.csv" records the performance of the neural network model when some components are silenced.
The first five columns (S1, D1, A1, S2, D2) represent the experimental conditions, corresponding to the synaptic weights, dendritic units, and axonal outputs of the first and second layers of the model.
The values in the columns indicate the number of removed units (for example, 1 represents the removal of 1 unit).
Starting from the sixth column, acc1 to acc20 are the experimental results, recording the specific accuracy rates obtained from 20 repeated tests under the current ablation conditions. 

The file "ablation_results_percentage.csv" is almost the same, it records the performance of the neural network model when different components suffer different proportions of silence.
The first five columns (S1, D1, A1, S2, D2) represent the experimental conditions, with the values indicating the percentage of removed units (for example, 10 represents the removal of 10%).
The Acc column after that corresponds to the specific accuracy rates obtained from multiple repeated tests.

